        "detailed_description": "<p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><strong>Galactic Gardener</strong> is a short-session roguelite about growing your own firepower. You pilot an autonomous terraforming drone left behind on a dead world, fighting back a mutation outbreak with weaponized plants.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Each run unfolds on a compact garden of <strong>planters</strong>, each holding up to <strong>six evolving plants</strong>. Between waves, you graft, link, and rearrange flora to forge deadly synergies — roots link shields, spores chain explosions, vines feed pulse cannons. Every placement matters, and every plant can turn against you.</p><ul class=\"bb_ul\"><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><strong>Grow your arsenal</strong> across a 2x3 grid of reactive ecosystems.</p></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><strong>Survive escalating waves</strong> of alien flora gone rogue.</p></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><strong>Stack links and mods</strong> that twist your build in unpredictable ways.</p></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><strong>Experiment with card-based upgrades</strong> that redefine your entire strategy each run.</p></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><strong>Chill yet chaotic tone</strong> — fast tactical gameplay wrapped in cozy bioluminescent visuals.</p></li></ul><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Humanity may have left, but your directive remains: <strong>Cultivate for their return.</strong> <br>The question is — what will still be alive when they do?</p>",
        "about_the_game": "<p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><strong>Galactic Gardener</strong> is a short-session roguelite about growing your own firepower. You pilot an autonomous terraforming drone left behind on a dead world, fighting back a mutation outbreak with weaponized plants.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Each run unfolds on a compact garden of <strong>planters</strong>, each holding up to <strong>six evolving plants</strong>. Between waves, you graft, link, and rearrange flora to forge deadly synergies — roots link shields, spores chain explosions, vines feed pulse cannons. Every placement matters, and every plant can turn against you.</p><ul class=\"bb_ul\"><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><strong>Grow your arsenal</strong> across a 2x3 grid of reactive ecosystems.</p></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><strong>Survive escalating waves</strong> of alien flora gone rogue.</p></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><strong>Stack links and mods</strong> that twist your build in unpredictable ways.</p></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><strong>Experiment with card-based upgrades</strong> that redefine your entire strategy each run.</p></li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><strong>Chill yet chaotic tone</strong> — fast tactical gameplay wrapped in cozy bioluminescent visuals.</p></li></ul><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Humanity may have left, but your directive remains: <strong>Cultivate for their return.</strong> <br>The question is — what will still be alive when they do?</p>",
